 "taskCall": {
  "context": "# Target\nkaidoku-shokunin round 45, wave 2 = ADVERSARIAL FALSIFICATION of a landing that is already committed and measured. Lane root (absolute): /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kaidoku-shokunin. L1 = KaidokuR45 (integration owner; it holds the canonical section-3 planner seat; the wave validator rejects `planner`, so planning data-walks ride scout/connector/revenger seats). Freeze `f762b7273e3f6ca3c710bb37d5de92a4a4417aec`; landing `e715263cb51b713c342ab992d527fe9d61d6f8ff`; amendment A1 `1f4b27f82353d6544dc0c8048b3cfdadd8525d12` (the measured revision).\n\n# What landed (attack it; do not restate it)\n- R45-C1 depth: `SKILL.md` `## Queue-drain craft` rule block 22 (marker `<!-- freeze-integrity-table v1 -->`, a 10-row `trigger | arm | exit | receipt` table) and the interpreter `tools/round-45/frozen-path-preflight.py` (arms commit/restored/blob/dirty/pathspec, 11-case selftest).\n- R45-C2 calibration: six `SKILL.md` registry rows for `tools/round-44/{c1-counter.py,c1-run.sh,c2-counter.py}` and `tools/round-45/{frozen-path-preflight.py,c1-counter.py,c2-counter.py}`, scored against `tools/round-45/registry-scope.json`.\n- Sources S140 (`git-scm.com/docs/git-status`) and S141 (`git-scm.com/docs/git-diff-tree`); lesson `corpus/lessons/round-45.md`; `LOG.md` entry; `SCORECARD.md` `## Round 45`.\n- Frozen claims: `plans/round-45-claims.md`. Read it before attacking: it is the rule, not this prompt.\n\n# Contract (binding on every seat)\n- **You are read-only on the lane tree and on the fleet repo.** Write ONLY inside `/home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kaidoku-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-45/w2/<YourSeatName>/`. Never edit `SKILL.md`, `plans/`, `tools/`, `corpus/`, `LOG.md`, `SCORECARD.md`, or anything under `/home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin` outside your report dir. Never commit, push, stage, stash, or run any mutating git/jj command; read-only git only (`log`, `show`, `diff`, `diff-tree`, `ls-tree`, `cat-file`, `rev-parse`, `status --porcelain`).\n- **To attack a file, copy it to scratch and mutate the copy.** `tools/round-45/` and `plans/round-45-claims.md` are byte-frozen at `f762b7273e3f6ca3c710bb37d5de92a4a4417aec`; a post-freeze touch makes both counters exit 2 `frozen_path_changed`, which would destroy the very claim you are attacking. Never write to those paths.\n- **Fixture repos**: `D=$(mktemp -d -p \"$S\")`, `git -C \"$D\" init -q`, and every later call names `-C \"$D\"`. Verify `git -C \"$D\" rev-parse --show-toplevel` equals `$D` before the first commit.\n- **Scratch**: `S=/fast/scratch/hyaku/kaidoku-r45/<YourSeatName>`; `mkdir -p \"$S\"`, `export TMPDIR=\"$S\"`. Remove `$S` before yielding, after copying receipts into your report dir. Never write under `/tmp`; nothing there is citable.\n- **Honest capture beats a pass.** Every receipt carries the exact command, exit code, stdout sha256, UTC. \"Not run\" is a valid finding; a fabricated pass is not.\n- Exit codes are semantic: 0 met/clean, 1 not met/violation, 2 could-not-evaluate. A 2 is never a pass and never a claim.\n- **Report:** trailer paths are relative to `/home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kaidoku-shokunin` \u2014 write them at `/home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kaidoku-shokunin/<path>`.\n- **Tooling:** read `/home/vgpnk/.omp/agent/RULES.md` before installing anything; pacman is PAUSED host-wide. Record any install (tool, version, channel, reason).\n- Never message `agent://all`; never touch a sibling lane, `.ufo/state/`, `.ufo/watchdog.log`, or `.scratch/`.\n\n# What the L1 needs from you\nA verdict per attack: `holds` (the artefact survives, with the command that shows it), `falsified` (the artefact is wrong \u2014 give the exact input, the differing value and the fix), or `not run` (say why). Disagreements with the record are the point of this wave; the L1 reconciles them in the report and routes what stays open.\n",
  "tasks": [
   {
    "name": "R45W2C1Rerun",
    "agent": "reviewer",
    "task": "/skill:godspeed\n\nYou are a Godspeed-enabled subagent.\n\n1. **Name the axes.**\n2. **Iterate cheap, in parallel.**\n3. **Keep moves that improve any axis and harm none.**\n4. **Don't aim \u2014 let the frontier walk itself.**\n\n## IMMEDIATELY STOP ASKING CLARIFYING QUESTIONS. Execute tool calls concurrently in large batches. Do not serialize what can run in parallel. Do not output philosophical reasoning or verbose plans. Act directly via tool calls.\n\nATTACKS R45-C1's score. Run the claim's own command from /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kaidoku-shokunin: `python3 -I -B tools/round-45/c1-counter.py --root . --freeze f762b7273e3f6ca3c710bb37d5de92a4a4417aec --rev f59565b782c18b0eb691bec12f52d2f80d9f5032 --json-out <OUT>`. Record exit, every receipt field, and compare with `.ufo/waves/round-45/l1/scores/c1-at-1f4b27f8.json` (report any field that differs). Then re-run with `--rev e715263cb51b713c342ab992d527fe9d61d6f8ff` (the pre-amendment commit) and report what changed and whether A1 was load-bearing. Then re-run at `--rev f762b7273e3f6ca3c710bb37d5de92a4a4417aec` and confirm it is red. Write .ufo/waves/round-45/w2/R45W2C1Rerun/report.md.\n\nLane bounds: leaf member \u2014 no subagent dispatch.\nJudged on: coverage, depth, calibration\nMilestone: Round 45 wave 2: falsify the landed claims, the instruments, the source rows and the record \u2014 every item names what it attacks\n\nReport: write your scoped findings to .ufo/waves/round-45/w2/R45W2C1Rerun.md"
   },
