    "task": "/skill:godspeed\n\nYou are a Godspeed-enabled subagent.\n\n1. **Name the axes.**\n2. **Iterate cheap, in parallel.**\n3. **Keep moves that improve any axis and harm none.**\n4. **Don't aim \u2014 let the frontier walk itself.**\n\n## IMMEDIATELY STOP ASKING CLARIFYING QUESTIONS. Execute tool calls concurrently in large batches. Do not serialize what can run in parallel. Do not output philosophical reasoning or verbose plans. Act directly via tool calls.\n\nATTACKS the axis verdicts. Run command A (the recipe in /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kaidoku-shokunin/SCORECARD.md `## Measurement recipes`) at `f59565b782c18b0eb691bec12f52d2f80d9f5032` and at `e715263cb51b713c342ab992d527fe9d61d6f8ff`. Report both JSONs: `knowledge_files`, `mapped`, `rule_blocks`, `citation_resolved_rules`, `coverage_score`, `depth_score`. The record claims 138/138 and 22/22 at the measured revision and says the landing alone read 21/22 before A1. Confirm or refute both numbers exactly. Then check that block 22's citation `corpus/knowledge/2026-10-25-r34b-pre-freeze-shortcut-replay-gate-stop.md:40-66` resolves at its file (line count \u2265 66) and that the cited lines actually discuss the gate's red/green cases. Write .ufo/waves/round-45/w2/R45W2CommandA/report.md.\n\nLane bounds: leaf member \u2014 no subagent dispatch except your single labrat.\nJudged on: coverage, depth, calibration\nMilestone: Round 45 wave 2: falsify the landed claims, the instruments, the source rows and the record \u2014 every item names what it attacks\n\nReport: write your scoped findings to .ufo/waves/round-45/w2/R45W2CommandA.md"
